    "problem_statement": "Sequential message parsing currently requires two separate steps to read an object at an offset range and then advance that range, with the risk of advancing after a failed read. A combined helper is needed that reads a buffer or an object from a message at a given offset range and, on success, advances the offset range by the number of bytes read (leaving it unchanged when the read fails). The DHCPv6 PD client unit test's message parser should be able to call this single read-and-advance helper in place of the read-plus-manual-advance pairs.",
